From: hawkff <109485367+hawkff@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 19:55:41 +0000
Subject: Show settings section headers in the primary color

Settings pages that group their rows into cards color their section
headers, such as "Basics" and "Advanced", with the color of row
summaries, and rely on the cards to set them apart. On dark backgrounds
the cards can have no visible edge, and with a black theme they are
black on black, so a header reads as one more row.

Use the primary color for those headers, as settings pages without
cards already do. Size, weight and spacing stay as they are: a smaller,
medium-weight label with space above it.

License: GPL-2.0-or-later - https://spdx.org/licenses/GPL-2.0-or-later.html

---
 .../browser_ui/styles/android/java/res/values/colors.xml      | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/components/browser_ui/styles/android/java/res/values/colors.xml b/components/browser_ui/styles/android/java/res/values/colors.xml
--- a/components/browser_ui/styles/android/java/res/values/colors.xml
+++ b/components/browser_ui/styles/android/java/res/values/colors.xml
@@ -35,7 +35,9 @@ found in the LICENSE file.
     <color name="bottom_system_nav_divider_color_light">@color/divider_color_light</color>
 
     <!-- Settings containment colors -->
-    <macro name="preference_category_text_color_contained">?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant</macro>
+    <!-- Section headers keep the primary color on grouped pages too: on dark and black
+         backgrounds the groups have no visible edge, and the summary color reads as a row. -->
+    <macro name="preference_category_text_color_contained">?attr/colorPrimary</macro>
     <macro name="preference_category_text_color_standard">?attr/colorPrimary</macro>
 
     <!-- This is the color that will appear on the system recents UI. It is a neutral background
--
